 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "离婚 \"to divorce\" takes no direct object: \"Have you decided to divorce?\" is 你们还是决定离婚吗, and \"divorce someone\" needs a preposition — 跟…离婚 — never 离婚 + person. Like 结婚, it's a \"separable\" verb: 了 or 过 can go between 离 and 婚, as in 已经离了婚的老陈 \"Lao Chen, already divorced.\" In speech the second syllable is often dropped: 两个人还想离 \"both still want to split up.\"",
